            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to release, then the Telugu for to free from captivity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: వెంబడించు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వెంబడించు — vembaḍiñcu — \"to pursue; to chase\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పోలీసులు దొంగను కారులో వెంబడించారు. pōlīsulu doṅganu kārulō vembaḍiñcāru. The police chased the thief in a car."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): వెంబడించాను, vembaḍiñcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వెంబడి means close behind; తరుము is the rougher, more spoken word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వెంబడించు (vembaḍiñcu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5488 lists Telugu vembaḍi, \"along with\", and vembaḍincu, under the word for \"the back\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
