          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దాక్కో — dākkō — \"to hide oneself\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దొంగ చెట్టు వెనక దాక్కున్నాడు. doṅga ceṭṭu venaka dākkunnāḍu. The thief hid behind a tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): దాక్కున్నాను, dākkunnānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దాచు is to hide a thing; దాక్కో (dākkō) is to hide yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దాక్కో (dākkō) is native Dravidian: DEDR 63 lists Telugu dāgu, \"to lie hidden\", beside dācu, \"to hide, conceal\"; దాక్కో adds the self-ending -kō."
            }
          ]
        },
